EXT. CROSSROADS SHRINE IN A PINE FOREST - TWILIGHT

A stone cairn at the meeting of four paths, crowned with offerings: ribbons, acorns, a child's wooden horse. Mist threads between the pines.

Four travellers arrive from four directions and stop, each at the edge of the clearing.

ARTEMISIA "ARTY" OKAFOR-LINDEN (30s, scout, hooded cloak, short bow) crouches beside the cairn and touches a ribbon.

BROTHER MALACHAI TREVELYAN-BOSE (50s, cleric, bronze bell hung at his belt) removes his hat in the shrine's presence.

KESTREL AMANI-DUNBAR (20s, thief, patched leathers, two daggers) leans on a pine, arms crossed, looking bored.

And SIR OSWALD PEMBERTON-ADEYEMI (40s, knight, tarnished armor, a battered shield with a painted sun) stands with his sword point-down in the loam.

OSWALD
Four roads, four travellers. I take it we all received the same summons.

ARTY
A black feather on the doorstep.

KESTREL
Same.

MALACHAI
A feather in the offering plate.

OSWALD
Mine was nailed to my gate.

KESTREL
Dramatic.

OSWALD
Quite.

ARTY
So who sent it?

MALACHAI
Not who. What.

KESTREL
Here we go.

MALACHAI
The shrine. The shrine called us.

KESTREL
Shrines don't call. They sit.

MALACHAI
This one speaks, if one listens.

OSWALD
Brother, let us listen, then.

Silence. A wind passes, bringing cold. The ribbons ripple. Arty cocks her head.

ARTY
Someone's coming.

Footsteps in the pines. The four draw weapons and turn together.

A small girl steps out of the mist. Perhaps nine. Ragged coat, bare feet, a black feather braided in her hair. She carries a wooden bowl.

GIRL
Hello.

OSWALD
Child. Where is your family?

GIRL
They're gone. I live here now.

KESTREL
Alone?

GIRL
With the roads.

MALACHAI
Child, did you send these feathers?

GIRL
(nodding)
Four of you. That's the right number.

ARTY
For what?

The girl sets down the bowl at the foot of the cairn. It is filled with dark water.

GIRL
To drink.

KESTREL
Pass.

GIRL
It's a promise.

OSWALD
What kind of promise?

GIRL
That you'll come back. After.

MALACHAI
After what?

The girl smiles, very faintly. The mist thickens. Behind the pines, something enormous exhales, and the ground trembles.

ARTY
(low)
Oswald.

OSWALD
I feel it.

KESTREL
Oh, great.

MALACHAI
Child, what is out there?

GIRL
That's what you're for.

The ground shudders again. Pinecones rattle down. Branches break. The four glance at one another. Then, one by one, they step to the bowl, dip their hands, and drink.

The water is cold as iron. Oswald coughs. Kestrel swears. Arty gasps and clutches her chest. Malachai rings his bell once, bright and clear.

Light blooms from the cairn. The mist retreats, trembling.

GIRL (CONT'D)
Thank you.

OSWALD
Child, what is your name?

GIRL
I don't have one yet.

She turns and walks into the pines. The four watch her go, then raise their weapons to the dark.

KESTREL
(muttering)
Should have taken the money.
